      "Most skincare frustration comes from a handful of repeatable mistakes rather than bad products: over-exfoliating and damaging the skin barrier, skipping sunscreen (especially on the belief that darker skin tones don't need it), layering too many active ingredients at once, using products meant for the wrong skin type, and expecting results within days instead of the 4-8 weeks most ingredients actually need. Fixing a routine usually means removing steps and slowing down, not adding more products — patch-test new actives, introduce one at a time, and treat sunscreen as non-negotiable given India's high year-round UV index.",
