    excerpt:
      "Applying products in the wrong order can cancel out their benefits entirely. Here's the exact sequence to follow, morning and night, for Indian skin.",
    summary:
      "The general rule for layering skincare is thinnest to thickest texture: cleanser, toner or essence, water-based serums (like vitamin C or niacinamide), spot treatments, eye cream, moisturizer, and — in the morning — sunscreen as the final step. Oil-based products always go after water-based ones, since oil forms a barrier that blocks anything applied on top from absorbing. Getting the order wrong doesn't just waste product; it can reduce how well active ingredients like vitamin C or retinol actually work, and applying sunscreen before other products blocks them from absorbing properly.",
