    excerpt: "'Cologne' means different things depending on who's using the word. Here's how the terms actually relate to each other, and why the confusion exists in the first place.",
    summary: "The confusion between perfume, cologne, and eau de toilette comes from 'cologne' being used two different ways — as a specific low-concentration category (Eau de Cologne) and as a casual, especially American, catch-all term for any men's fragrance regardless of actual concentration.",
